# Build a character who actually HOLDS a prestige class, and photograph what
# the engine gives him.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. bd inc-tek.8.3 corrected the level tables printed by five
# prestige classes, the Sentinel among them: its prose listed the save columns
# in the wrong order, so the table promised a good Fortitude save the class
# does not grant and a poor Reflex save it does. tools/check_prestige_tables.sh
# proves the corrected TABLE is on screen. It cannot prove the table is RIGHT,
# because it never makes a Sentinel -- it only reads the menu description.
#
# This script makes one. The character sheet then breaks every save down by
# class -- "Fortitude +2 (Rogue +1/ Sentinel +1)" -- so the engine states the
# prestige class's own contribution, separately, in numbers. That is the
# oracle, and tools/check_sentinel_live.sh compares it against the table.
#
# WHY IT COULD NOT BE WRITTEN BEFORE. Every step below that picks something is
# named rather than counted, and three of them had no counted equivalent worth
# writing (bd inc-cso):
#
#   * The Skill Manager has no menu letters, and the Sentinel wants Listen,
#     Spot and Search at 10. Counting DOWN to a skill breaks the moment a
#     class list changes, and spends the ranks somewhere else in silence.
#   * Levelling a multiclass character opens two menus that appear only at
#     some levels -- "Which class do you wish to advance in?" and the feat
#     list. A fixed run of G keystrokes desynchronises on the first one and
#     then picks feats at random with the leftovers. That is not a guess: a
#     run of "G*12" reached level 7, and a bare @until pressing G reached 11
#     of a wanted 13 before giving up, because 'g' is itself a valid menu
#     letter and kept choosing things.
#   * The prestige list must be entered by name. Its letters are positions in
#     a list built from lib/prestige.irh.
#
# SEED. The attribute rolls and the offered feats vary with the seed, so the
# two chargen feat picks stay positional and a seed is passed.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Rogue"
a                       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets
@choose "Neutral"
@choose "Alertness"     # the Sentinel requires this feat
@until "Unspent Skill Ranks" a          # however many feats are asked for

# Eighteen ranks, two to a skill. The three the Sentinel cares about first;
# the rest only because character generation will not let go of a character
# with a rank unspent. UP and DOWN both work -- the Skill Manager does not
# wrap, so the names are given in the direction of travel.
@cursorto:mark "Listen" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Searching" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Spot" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Lockpicking" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Intuition" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Bluff" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Alchemy" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Appraise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

y       # Do you wish to worship Maeve? -- yes. An elf is given Maeve at birth
        #   anyway (lib/races.irh:1144-1147); the Twilight Huntsman is the
        #   prestige class that needs her, not this one.
a       # Personality archetype

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

d                               # character sheet
@until "Class  Rogue 5" G       # five core levels, for the ranks they carry

# Top the three sensory skills up to their maximum. The class wants each at
# 10, and ISkillLevel (src/Create.cpp:3955) counts training and the inherent
# attribute bonus as well as ranks, so eight ranks clears it.
S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Listen" DOWN
RIGHT*8
@cursorto:mark "Searching" DOWN
RIGHT*8
@cursorto:mark "Spot" DOWN
RIGHT*8
ENTER y

P                               # [P]restige Classes
@expect "Choose a class:"
@choose "Sentinel"
@dump:taken

# Four Sentinel levels, which is as far as the printed table is checked.
# @until presses G through whatever the level-up asks first; @choose answers
# the class question by name; @while clears a feat menu when one appears.
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Sentinel"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Sentinel"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Sentinel"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Sentinel"
@while "Choose a feat" a

@expect "Sentinel 4"
@dump:sentinel4
W                       # Write Dump
s h e e t ENTER         # filename: "sheet"
ESC
@quit
